<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abarsal</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abarsal was an ancient city-state of the twenty-fourth century BCE known from the archives of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ebla">Ebla</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>. A treaty between Ebla and Abarsal, preserved on a clay tablet, is one of the oldest known international agreements, setting out rules on boundaries, trade and the treatment of envoys and fugitives. The location of Abarsal is uncertain; scholars have placed it on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euphrates">Euphrates</a> or in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a>.</p></div>
